<spell-page "diagram usage" notebook>
	<header level="1">
		Diagram
		<header>Boxes in columns and the links between them:  a NERD, an ERD, any boxes-and-lines picture, drawn by the NERD skill's rules.</>
	</>
	<section>
		<toolbar class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#using-it">Using it</>
			<item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
			<item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  how to use it (attributes in practice, events, framework snippets), keyboard, accessibility. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			Give it a spec:  the `spec` property, or a `<script type="application/json">` child on a static page.
			The spec is the NERD skill's JSON as it is, so a NERD written for that skill's script opens here:

			- `columns`, left to right, each a stack of `groups`;  a group has a `label`, a `color`, and `nodes`
			  (one stack) or `lanes` (stacks side by side);  `{ "legend": true }` places the legend
			- a node has a `name`, a `note`, its linking `fields` (or example `bullets`), and its own `color`
			- `edges`, each `{ "from": "Box.field", "to": "Other", "kind": "contains" }` (solid) or `"ref"` (dashed,
			  the default);  a field `{ "name": "x", "derived": true }` is drawn italic, `x (derived)`
			- `gap_before` on a group or node lines it up with what links to it

			Or a flat `{ nodes, edges }`:  it's put in at most `columns` columns (3 by default).

			Drag a box to move it;  `remember="name"` keeps where each person put them, and Put back forgets.
			`fixed` stops moving boxes.  Each box takes focus, and the arrow keys move it (Shift for bigger steps);  Enter is a click.  A right click opens a menu:  Put back, Save as SVG, Save as JSON;  from script, `toSVG()`, `saveSVG()` and `saveJSON()`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```js
			const diagram = document.querySelector("ui-diagram")
			diagram.spec = { columns: [...], edges: [...] }
			diagram.addEventListener("ui-node-clicked", (event) => console.log(event.detail.name))
			diagram.addEventListener("ui-node-moved", (event) => console.log(event.detail))
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			| Key | What it does |
			| --- | --- |
			| Tab | Moves to the next box |
			| Arrow keys | Move the box a little;  with Shift, further |
			| Enter or Space | A click on the box (a NERD box turns over) |
			| Shift F10 or the menu key | Opens the menu:  Put back, Save as SVG, Save as JSON |
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			The drawing is a group (`role="group"`), named by how many boxes and links it has:  "Diagram:  9 boxes,
			11 links".  Each box is a button named by its name, its description saying the arrow keys move it;
			its fields are real text in it.  A page that relies on the diagram should
			say what it shows in words too.
		</>
	</>
</spell-page>
